-- title:
--   Unique place of the Igusa field above a supersingular valuation
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $\kappa$ a perfect field of characteristic $p$, let $M \geq 5$ be a nonzero natural number with $p \nmid M$, and let $w$ be an integral weight-one form of level $M$ over $\kappa$: a modular form of weight $1$ for $\Gamma_1(M)$ together with a power series over $\mathbb{Z}$ whose complex reduction is its $q$-expansion and whose reduction $\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,\kappa$ into $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,\kappa$ is nonzero; write $a = w.\mathrm{hasseRootFn}$ for the inverse of that reduction. Put $K_0 = \mathrm{x1FunctionFieldC}\,\kappa\,M$, the $\kappa$-subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,\kappa$ generated by the ratios of integral $q$-expansions for $\Gamma_1(M)$, and $\mathrm{Ig} = \mathrm{igusaFunctionFieldX1C}\,\kappa\,M\,w$, the $\kappa$-subfield generated by $K_0 \cup \{a\}$, so $K_0 \leq \mathrm{Ig}$. Let $\bar\jmath \in K_0$ be the element whose underlying Laurent series is $\mathrm{jqModC}\,\kappa = q^{-1}\cdot(\text{reduction of } \mathrm{jNum})$, and let $O$ be a valuation subring of $K_0$ containing the image of $\kappa$, with $O \neq \top$ and $\bar\jmath \in O$. Assume that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $p$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi : O \to \Omega$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal of $O$, the value $\varphi(\bar\jmath)$ lies in $\mathrm{ssJSet}\,p\,\Omega$, i.e. every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with that $j$-invariant has no nonzero point killed by $p$. Then: (i) any two valuation subrings $O_1, O_2$ of $\mathrm{Ig}$ whose contractions along the inclusion $K_0 \hookrightarrow \mathrm{Ig}$ equal $O$ are equal; and (ii) there is a valuation subring $O'$ of $\mathrm{Ig}$ contracting to $O$ such that every $e \in O'$ differs from the image of some $f \in O$ by a nonunit of $O'$.
--
--   This is Igusa's theorem that the Igusa covering is totally ramified over the supersingular points of $X_1(M)$, in the language of valuation subrings of function fields: above a supersingular place of $K_0$ there is exactly one place of the Igusa field, and the residue extension there is trivial. Unlike the Kummer-theoretic lemma it invokes, the conclusion records only uniqueness, existence and triviality of the residue extension, and not the uniformiser relation expressing the ramification index $p-1$. It is used in the analysis of integral models of the Igusa curve over the supersingular locus.
